{"body":"### V2 short-circuit creates unnecessary no-op commit

**Low Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
When the content hash matches in the v2 `updateCommittedFullTranscript` short-circuit, the code still performs `spliceCheckpointSubtree` + `updateRef`, creating a new commit and advancing the `/full/current` ref even though the tree content is identical. The v1 equivalent in `replaceTranscript` correctly just does `return nil`, avoiding unnecessary tree surgery, commit creation, and ref update. Since entries are unmodified, the splice reconstructs the same tree, making this a pure no-op commit. On re-finalize with N checkpoints, this creates N unnecessary commits on `/full/current`.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

